# The shell scripts are authored on Windows but run inside a Linux container.
# Without this, a CRLF checkout makes the shebang unparseable and the container
# exits with "no such file or directory", naming the interpreter.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# The world seed is game data, not source: git must not touch a byte of it. The
# .vx2 voxel files are gzip streams that end-of-line conversion would corrupt,
# and the .sbc / .sbs files are written by the game with its own encoding. Diffs
# on a 2.6 MB sector file would be unreadable anyway.
server/world-seed/** binary
